(*"product_concept_schema.concept_feature_operator"
A *concept_feature_operator* is a definition of an operation that is used to constrain the relationship between two <<express:product_concept_schema.product_concept_feature,product_concept_feature>>. 

[example]
====
"AND", "NOT", and "OR" are *concept_feature_operator* names.
====

[NOTE]
--
The meaning of the operation and the list of allowed values for the *name* attribute can be specified in each annotated EXPRESS schema that uses or specializes this entity or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
--

[NOTE]
--
Annex E contains examples of this entity and figures that depict the relationships between it and the other entities of this schema.
--
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.concept_feature_operator.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the *concept_feature_operator* is known.

[NOTE]
--
The name designates the operation.
--
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.concept_feature_operator.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the *concept_feature_operator*. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.concept_feature_relationship"
A *concept_feature_relationship* is an association between two <<express:product_concept_schema.product_concept_feature,product_concept_feature>>. 

[NOTE]
--
The meaning of the association can be specified in each annotated EXPRESS schema that uses or specializes this entity or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
--
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.concept_feature_relationship.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the *concept_feature_relationship* is known.
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.concept_feature_relationship.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the *concept_feature_relationship*. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.concept_feature_relationship.relating_product_concept_feature"
one of the <<express:product_concept_schema.product_concept_feature,product_concept_feature>> that is a part of the association.
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.concept_feature_relationship.related_product_concept_feature"
the other <<express:product_concept_schema.product_concept_feature,product_concept_feature>> that is a part of the association. If one element of the relationship is dependent upon the other, this attribute shall be the dependent one.
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.concept_feature_relationship_with_condition"
A *concept_feature_relationship_with_condition* is a type of <<express:product_concept_schema.concept_feature_relationship,concept_feature_relationship>> in which a conditional operator characterizes the relationship between the <<express:product_concept_schema.concept_feature_relationship.related_product_concept_feature,related_product_concept_feature>> and the <<express:product_concept_schema.concept_feature_relationship.relating_product_concept_feature,relating_product_concept_feature>>. 

[NOTE]
--
When specified as the condition for a <<express:product_concept_schema.conditional_concept_feature,conditional_concept_feature>>, a *concept_feature_relationship_with_condition* defines a constraint for the use of a <<express:product_concept_schema.product_concept_feature,product_concept_feature>>. Complex conditions can be constructed for a <<express:product_concept_schema.product_concept_feature,product_concept_feature>> by using the *concept_feature_relationship_with_condition* to relate <<express:product_concept_schema.conditional_concept_feature,conditional_concept_feature>> to each other.
--

[NOTE]
--
Annex E contains examples of this entity and figures that depict the relationships between it and the other entities of this schema.
--
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.concept_feature_relationship_with_condition.conditional_operator"
the <<express:product_concept_schema.concept_feature_operator,concept_feature_operator>> used in the relationship between the <<express:product_concept_schema.concept_feature_relationship.relating_product_concept_feature,relating_product_concept_feature>> and the <<express:product_concept_schema.concept_feature_relationship.related_product_concept_feature,related_product_concept_feature>>.

[example]
====
A condition of negation is specified by using a <<express:product_concept_schema.concept_feature_operator,concept_feature_operator>> with a name of "NOT" and a *product_concept_feature_relationship_with_condition* in which the <<express:product_concept_schema.concept_feature_relationship.related_product_concept_feature,related_product_concept_feature>> and the <<express:product_concept_schema.concept_feature_relationship.relating_product_concept_feature,relating_product_concept_feature>> reference the same instance of <<express:product_concept_schema.product_concept_feature,product_concept_feature>>.
====
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.conditional_concept_feature"
A *conditional_concept_feature* is a type of <<express:product_concept_schema.product_concept_feature,product_concept_feature>> that is the combination of two <<express:product_concept_schema.product_concept_feature,product_concept_feature>> constrained by an operator. 

[NOTE]
--
Complex combinations of <<express:product_concept_schema.product_concept_feature,product_concept_feature>> may be constructed using *conditional_concept_feature*s as operands of a <<express:product_concept_schema.concept_feature_relationship_with_condition,concept_feature_relationship_with_condition>>.
--

[NOTE]
--
Annex E contains examples of this entity and figures that depict the relationships between it and the other entities of this schema.
--
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.conditional_concept_feature.condition"
the <<express:product_concept_schema.concept_feature_relationship_with_condition,concept_feature_relationship_with_condition>> that establishes the condition for the *conditional_concept_feature*.
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.product_concept"
A *product_concept* is a type of product as specified in ISO 10303-41 that is defined by a producer to satisfy potential or actual customer requirements. 

[NOTE]
--
A *product_concept* will often correspond to the highest level item(s) manufactured by an organization for a customer. It may be characterized by a set of product features identified by the customers or derived from customers' needs. The definition of product concepts is often driven by market and customer requirements and forecasting.
--

[example]
====
If an organization manufactures cars and engines for cars, the cars will be represented by *product_concept* instances. If another organization manufactures engines for cars, the engines will be represented as *product_concept*s in that organization.
====
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.product_concept.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the *product_concept*.

[example]
====
The *id* could be a sales model number.
====
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.product_concept.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the *product_concept* is known.
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.product_concept.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the *product_concept*. The value of this attribute need not be specified.

[NOTE]
--
This attribute can be used to convey the purpose, functionality, and selected features for the *product_concept*.
--
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.product_concept.market_context"
the frame of reference in which the *product_concept* is defined.

[NOTE]
--
The frame of reference for the *product_concept* is not restricted to a market context. To be upwardly compatible with *product_concept* as specified in ISO 10303:1994, the name of the *market_context* attribute is unchanged.
--

[NOTE]
--
The value of the *market_context* attribute can be constrained in each annotated EXPRESS schema that uses or specializes this entity data type or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
--
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.product_concept.ur:UR1"
The *id* shall be unique within a population of *product_concept*.
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.product_concept_feature"
A *product_concept_feature* is a characteristic intended to be used to distinguish variations among the products of one or more <<express:product_concept_schema.product_concept,product_concept>>. 

[example]
====
"Luxury equipment" is a characteristic that distinguishes between a standard, low-price car and a topclass car.
====

[NOTE]
--
The categorization of *product_concept_feature*s is accomplished through the mechanisms defined in ISO 10303-41 for collecting product data into groups. The name of the group indicates the category of the collected items.
--
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.product_concept_feature.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the *product_concept_feature*.
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.product_concept_feature.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the *product_concept_feature* is known.
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.product_concept_feature.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the *product_concept_feature*. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.product_concept_feature_association"
A *product_concept_feature_association* is a relationship, that relates a <<express:product_concept_schema.product_concept_feature,product_concept_feature>> to a <<express:product_concept_schema.product_concept,product_concept>>. A <<express:product_concept_schema.product_concept_feature,product_concept_feature>> as it is related to a <<express:product_concept_schema.product_concept,product_concept>> may define the content of a <<express:configuration_management_schema.configuration_item,configuration_item>>. 

[NOTE]
--
The meaning of the association can be specified in each annotated EXPRESS schema that uses or specializes this entity or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
--
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.product_concept_feature_association.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the *product_concept_feature_association* is known.
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.product_concept_feature_association.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the *product_concept_feature_association*. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.product_concept_feature_association.concept"
the <<express:product_concept_schema.product_concept,product_concept>> that is being associated.
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.product_concept_feature_association.feature"
the <<express:product_concept_schema.product_concept_feature,product_concept_feature>> that is being associated.
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.product_concept_relationship"
A *product_concept_relationship* is an association between two <<express:product_concept_schema.product_concept,product_concept>>. 

[NOTE]
--
The meaning of the association can be specified in each annotated EXPRESS schema that uses or specializes this entity or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
--
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.product_concept_relationship.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the *product_concept_relationship* is known.
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.product_concept_relationship.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the *product_concept_relationship*. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.product_concept_relationship.relating_product_concept"
one of the <<express:product_concept_schema.product_concept,product_concept>> that is a part of the association.
*)

(*"product_concept_schema.product_concept_relationship.related_product_concept"
the other <<express:product_concept_schema.product_concept,product_concept>> that is a part of the association. If one element of the relationship is dependent upon the other, this attribute shall be the dependent one.
*)
